WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.995
Learn's page, Integrate Key
Vault with Azure Private Link,

3
00:00:04.995 --> 00:00:09.112
is blunt about where private
endpoints fail: name resolution.

4
00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:13.916
The private D N S zone has to exist
and be linked to the virtual network,

5
00:00:13.916 --> 00:00:18.551
it has to hold the record, and
on-premises D N S has to forward to Azure.

6
00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:23.188
Miss any of the three and clients
quietly keep using the public address.

7
00:00:23.188 --> 00:00:26.908
And the vault: Learn's page,
Secure your Azure Key Vault,

8
00:00:26.908 --> 00:00:32.658
recommends role-based access, not legacy
access policies; pim for administrators;

9
00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.364
purge protection; rotation; audit logs;

10
00:00:35.364 --> 00:00:39.000
and private endpoints with
public access disabled.

11
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.686
So this module builds central private
D N S, turns public access off,

12
00:00:43.686 --> 00:00:46.839
and puts each vault
behind role-based access,

13
00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:51.580
with purge protection, a closed
firewall, rotation and an audit log.
